{"name":"Bunker","hex":"#292c2f","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Bunker","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Bunker"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bunker","blocks":[{"text":"A bunker is a defensive fortification designed to protect people and valued materials from falling bombs, artillery, or other attacks. Bunkers are almost always underground, in contrast to blockhouses which are mostly above ground. They were used extensively in World War I, World War II, and the Cold War for weapons facilities, command and control centers, storage facilities, etc. Bunkers can also be used as protection from tornadoes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Augarten_Flakturm_Wien2008a.jpg/330px-Augarten_Flakturm_Wien2008a.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bunker"},{"title":"Bunker (2026 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Bunker is a 2026 psychological thriller film written and directed by Florian Zeller. It stars Penélope Cruz, Javier Bardem, Stephen Graham, Paul Dano, and Patrick Schwarzenegger."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bunker_(2026_film)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/NORADNorth-Portal.jpg/500px-NORADNorth-Portal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/NORADNorth-Portal.jpg/1280px-NORADNorth-Portal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/NORADNorth-Portal.jpg/500px-NORADNorth-Portal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The north entrance to the Cheyenne Mountain Complex in Colorado, United States","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANORADNorth-Portal.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://th